          "text": "Abraham’s laughter and concern for Ishmael do not end with Ishmael’s exclusion from blessing. God promises to bless, make fruitful, and multiply Ishmael, while specifying that the covenant will be established through Isaac, Sarah’s promised son. Abraham then carries out the circumcision command for his household that same day, joining an astonished response to the promise with immediate action.",
